alex smith  suffered a serious broken leg during the  2018  season infection that that nearly  claimed his life and he has worked his  way back worked his way  back he said last week he's cleared for  football activities he still hasn't  passed a physical  in washington they're taking their time  with him yesterday peter  quarterbacks coach ken zampeezy had some  very positive things to say about alex  smith his attitude how he learns and  what it's going to take to get him back  on the field can he protect himself  they're going to watch him in drills  watch him in 11 on 11 what does he do  when a guy breaks through can he move  away like he used to  but if this guy still has it physically  he's only 36. now 36 used to be old  as quarterbacks went not anymore not  with tom brady turning 43 in three days  i'm fascinated by the possibility in  this year  with everything that is in turmoil and  you look at what alex smith did with the  49ers in 2011  in the lockout year when the 49ers were  supposedly rebuilding and jim harbaugh  was in his first year as head coach  and the 49ers were within a muffed punt  or two of making it to the super bowl  you got ron rivera new coach trying to  stabilize things  if alex smith is healthy enough to  protect himself and play like he did  before the injury and i know that's a  big if  i i don't know how you don't give him  every chance to win that starting job  over dwayne haskins especially for this  year  you know the washington quarterback  situation is absolutely fascinating  you got the starter for ron rivera in  carolina last year  who when they brought him in this year  i just said well you know i i i my  feeling is he's got a better chance to  start  than dwayne haskins when there's no off  season activity because rivera knows him  better  now you get alex smith and you basically  i i i said this to uh a  talk show guy down there the other day  but i said that  this is really of all the amazing  stories happening right now  in the nfl this is the most amazing  for alex smith after watching that  stefania bell espn  incredible e60 story  uh about with cameras in the room  looking at his leg that i could have  sworn they were going to have to  amputate his leg  and now he's on the active slash  physically unable to perform list  for for people who don't know exactly  what that means  let me tell you he can do everything  that any player can  can do in practice over the next month  other than to practice okay  so but he can do everything else he can  run he can lift he can do all the drills  you know he can be in the one-on-ones  and  and  all this stuff he can i mean he can  throw my whole thing is  it's amazing to me that he's gotten this  far and  mike you're right i don't assume he's  gonna win this job  but the fact that he's even in  competition  he's even a thought for this job to me  is amazing  yeah i i cannot believe it it's a great  story even if he never puts a helmet on  again  but the idea that that he's on the  verge of being cleared to practice and  that they're going to evaluate him  carefully and see if he can still play  like he used to  i mean look this is a guy who has been  through  offensive coordinator after offensive  coordinator um  and to the point where the offensive  coordinator  now in washington scott turner is the  son  of the guy who was alex smith's  offensive coordinator his second year in  the league back in 2006  norv turner so he's learned offenses  he's relearned offense he's  unlearned offenses he's he's always  found a way to get it  done and starting in 2011 that year with  the 49ers  he became a better quarterback you know  it was a good five six seasons before he  emerged  as a guy that we look at as a top half  of the nfl quarterback  and then he got to kansas city and it  worked out very well for the  for the chiefs with alex smith until  they decided to go all in for patrick  mahomes  and even then smith had a great final  season in kansas city so you know  you take that broken leg out of the mix  and alex smith is still going strong as  the starting quarterback in washington  and maybe jay gruden is still the head  coach they were six and four i believe  when smith got injured in 2018 which is  you know better than most washington  teams have been over the past 21 years  that daniel snyder's owned the franchise  so  i just look i i root for great stories  and this is nothing against wayne  haskins who may have a very long  and productive and successful career and  by all indications he's checking all the  boxes this off season  he's rising to the challenge that was  created for him by ron rivera  but man it's hard not to root for alex  smith to get back on the field and play  like he used to play and  really put the capper on one of the most  inspiring stories we've ever seen  you know two things about what you just  said number one  isn't it amazing that um after alex  smith has one of the best 10 seasons  in football in 2017  uh andy reid and brett veach trade them  because  essentially they want to play a kid who  they've only seen one game  the one game he played against denver i  find that  to be uh you know someday when andy reid  i assume he'll go into canton but  someday when andy reid goes into canton  that'll be a story i will long remember  about  there's more to coaching a football team  than just coaching and there's decisions  that you have to make  and that was a great one but the other  one i would say is  alex smith at his peak has been  a truly underrated player his playoff  duel with drew brees  uh you know in san francisco a few years  ago  when joe staley gets out on the edge and  has the best  pulling run block for a quarterback i  think i've ever  seen in my life you know when alex smith  runs around for  for the touchdown that game where he  went absolutely  toe to toe with a transcendent  quarterback in drew brees  how great he was that day how great he  was in 2000 2017  with 